<title>USA: Reliance Acceptance Q1 loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Reliance Acceptance Q1 loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>SAN ANTONIO, Texas 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			 1996</p>
<p> Oper Shr    loss$0.76	    profit$0.21</p>
<p> Oper Net    loss9,900	    profit3,200</p>
<p> Net Int. Income 14,406		   11,208</p>
<p> Avg Shrs	  13,052		   15,366</p>
<p>	 (All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: The loss for the quarter was attributed to a provision for credit losses of $22.2 million in the 1997 quarter, which served to boost the company's total reserves for  possiblie credit losses from 4.1 percent of finance receivables at December 31, 1996 to 7.5 percent at March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>The company reported net income for the first quarter at $37.6 million compared with $6.9 million for the year-ago period, after a gain from a split-off of discontinued operations.</p>
